  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>D</p>\n<p>The total energy in simple harmonic motion is given by E = (1/2) * m * ω^2 * <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{0}\"></span>^2. The angular frequency ω can be found from the period T using ω = 2π/T. Substituting the given values (m=1.0 kg, T=2.0 s, E=72 J) yields an amplitude <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x_{0}\"></span> = 12/π ≈ 3.8 m.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.0\\,\\mathrm{kg}\"></span> mass undergoes undamped simple harmonic motion with a period of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\\,\\mathrm{s}\"></span>. The total energy is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"72\\,\\mathrm{J}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the amplitude?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"15\\,\\mathrm{m}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"12\\,\\mathrm{m}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"7.6\\,\\mathrm{m}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.8\\,\\mathrm{m}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
